userStories.description:
**Goal** — Reach a dedicated CI repair builder from real workflow dispatch and carry failed/skipped step facts into findings while extracting the full CI repair seam without cycles.

**Motivation** — The repair runs the branch-fix prompt ("You are fixing a feature branch after its whole-branch review") under the `wf-branch-fix` role.

**Approach** — 4. **CI repair prompt.** `buildWorkflowCiRepairPrompt` (`src/prompts/builders/workflow-ci-repair-builder.ts`) is the CI repair's brief, and includes `REPAIR_VERIFICATION_RULE` (US-002). `FeatureSteps.branchFix` takes `opts.ciRound?: number`. When it is set, `buildFeatureEnv` passes `runBranchFix` `ciRepair: { round, prUrl? }`, and `runBranchFix` builds the CI repair prompt instead of the branch-fix prompt. Final-gate repair keeps the branch-fix prompt. `ciRepairFindingsOf` puts the step facts into each finding's `issue`: with a `failedStep`, the issue is `CI check <name> failed at step "<step>".`, then (only when `skippedSteps` is non-empty) a line `Steps CI skipped after it, which never ran: <a>, <b>`, then the excerpt, each separated by one newline. Without a `failedStep` the issue stays `CI check <name> failed:
<excerpt>`.

5. **Moving the CI repair out of `feature-steps.ts`.** That file is at 597 of its 600-line limit.
- `ciRepairStep`, `ciRepairDecision`, `readCiFailuresForRepair` and `ciRepairFindingsOf` move to `src/workflow/ci-repair-steps.ts`.
- `feature-steps.ts` re-exports `ciRepairStep` and `ciRepairDecision`, so `feature-graph.ts` and the existing tests import them unchanged.
- The shared helpers the moved code needs (`DEFAULT_LIMITS`, `limitsOf`, `costExceeded`, `NO_MIRROR`, `featureStep`, `roundLabel`; `featureStep` also needs `FEATURE_SCOPE` from `./advisor-live`) are all defined in `feature-steps.ts` and used by code that stays there, so they move to a third module, `src/workflow/feature-step-helpers.ts`, which both files import. `feature-steps.ts` keeps re-exporting `featureStep` and `NO_MIRROR`. `ci-repair-steps.ts` must not import `feature-steps.ts`: the import-cycle baseline is 0 (`bun run check:import-cycles`).

**Scope** — In: the dedicated builder and prompts barrel, ciRound forwarding, runBranchFix's ciRepair prompt selection, ciRepairStep round forwarding, step-aware finding issue text, and the two workflow module extractions. Out: creating the repair role/op (US-001), routing/basic shared rule (US-002), reading step metadata (US-003), concern/target persistence (US-005), terminal classification (US-006), review builds (US-007). Workflow final-gate repair changes its session role to `wf-repair` but keeps the branch-fix prompt.

**Interface** — Verbatim target builder:
```typescript
// src/prompts/builders/workflow-ci-repair-builder.ts (exported from @/prompts), US-004
export function buildWorkflowCiRepairPrompt(input: {
  readonly round: number;
  readonly prUrl?: string;
  readonly specPath?: string;
  readonly prdPath?: string;
  readonly reportPath: string;
  readonly findings: readonly WorkflowPromptFinding[];
}): string;
```
`BranchFixInput` gains `ciRepair?: { readonly round: number; readonly prUrl?: string }`. `FeatureSteps.branchFix` target is `(findings, opts?: { readonly prUrl?: string; readonly repair?: true; readonly ciRound?: number })`.

**Prompt contract** — Include the exact fix-forward rule `Never skip, disable or ignore a failing check, and never edit the CI configuration to make it pass.` and reproduction rule `A CI job stops at its first failing step, so a step CI skipped never ran: reproduce the failing step and every skipped step locally.` Render all findings with renderWorkflowFindings, include spec/PRD paths when supplied, append a round-labelled CI repair section to the writable report, retain WORKFLOW_ARTIFACTS_RULE and WORKFLOW_REPLY_CONTRACT, and include REPAIR_VERIFICATION_RULE. CI brief must not describe a whole-branch review. Preserve explicit input.prompt overrides.

**Implementation and test notes** — Drive buildFeatureEnv with repair: true, ciRound: 2 and a PR URL through makeScriptedCallOp to the actual builder. Drive the failed/skipped-step seam through publishStep with a stub readCiFailures rather than testing an isolated copy. US-002's CI URL expectation gains ciRound: 1; the no-URL CI expectation also gains ciRound: 1 while the gate-with-url case stays unchanged. The extraction's typecheck, import-cycle and file-size checks are structural verification, not behavioral acceptance criteria. The story-local outOfScope entry excludes only expressing those structural checks as ACs; both module extractions and their re-exports remain required implementation scope.
